  "instance_name": "black_friday",
  "label": "Black Friday",
  "description": "An annual shopping event in the United States that occurs on the day after Thanksgiving, known for large discounts and heavy consumer spending. The term 'Black Friday' originally referred to the day when retailers' books went from a 'red' (loss) to a 'black' (profit) balance. The meme uses this commercial event to create a racially charged and offensive juxtaposition with the historical trauma of slavery, leveraging the word 'black' to reference both the racial identity of enslaved people and the color associated with the sale.",
